## 3. Local vs optional cloud, and privacy implications

| Capability | Default | Cloud option | Privacy implication |
|---|---|---|---|
| Chat generation | Local LLM | Optional, per-conversation | Cloud sees the assembled prompt, which may include retrieved memory unless redacted |
| Embeddings / retrieval | Local | Optional | Sending text to embed leaks content in bulk; keep local by default |
| Speech-to-text | Local | Optional | Cloud STT means raw audio leaves the device — highest-sensitivity egress |
| Text-to-speech | Local | Optional | Cloud TTS sends reply text off-device |
| Avatar & VRM assets | Fully local | None | Assets stay on device; no reason to cloud them |
| Memory store | Local, encrypted | Optional sync (future) | Sync would move the most private data; default off, per-category |
| Desktop tools | Local | None | Never delegate OS actions to a cloud service |
| Image / media generation | Local small model or off | Optional | Prompts can reveal intent; treat as sensitive |
| Persona/settings sync | Local | Optional | Low sensitivity, but still opt-in |
| Telemetry | Off | Off | Only ever aggregate and opt-in; never include content |

**Rule of thumb:** if a feature can run locally at acceptable quality, it runs locally and cloud is an explicit, per-request upgrade. The Egress Gateway enforces this at the network boundary rather than relying on UI copy.

