## 6. Existing Electron project vs CREAO-hosted services

### Implementable entirely in the existing Electron project (no CREAO dependency)
- Phases 0–5 in full: chat, memory, voice, avatar, desktop tools, permissions, asset vault, audit log, local model runtime.
- The Egress Gateway and Consent store.
- Encryption at rest, export/delete, and all local UI.

This is the whole product's core. LocalCore can ship and be fully useful with **zero** CREAO-hosted services.

### Requires CREAO-hosted services (only if you want them — all optional)
- **Model & asset distribution** — a CDN-backed store for model weights and VRM/voice assets.
- **Account sync** — personas and settings across devices (memory and media excluded by default).
- **Cloud inference proxy** — a managed path to cloud models, with policy and cost controls.
- **Character marketplace** — sharing and discovering personas (Phase 6+).
- **Licensing / entitlement** — if any content is commercial.
- **Opt-in telemetry aggregation** — never content, only coarse health metrics.

**Boundary rule:** nothing in Phases 0–5 should require a CREAO account. If a feature needs a server, it belongs to Phase 6 and must degrade gracefully to local-only.

